2026-09-24 (later, before any timed HGTO run): duplicate Intel OpenMP runtime fixed in env `hgto`.
Symptom: every HGTO run that calls PARDISO after importing torch (HGTO's own `hgto run --method oc`, and the final
independent evaluation of every run) aborted with "OMP: Error #15: Initializing libiomp5md.dll, but found
libiomp5md.dll already initialized". torch 2.11.0+cu128 ships Lib/site-packages/torch/lib/libiomp5md.dll; the pip MKL
used by pypardiso loads Library/bin/libiomp5md.dll, so two OpenMP runtimes were loaded in one process.
Fix: renamed Lib/site-packages/torch/lib/libiomp5md.dll -> libiomp5md.dll.bak_duplicate_openmp. torch's loader then
resolves libiomp5md.dll from <env>/Library/bin (it adds that folder to the DLL search path), so torch and MKL share one
runtime. Check: torch float64 matmul with 2 threads and a pypardiso solve in one process succeed; the loaded module is
C:\Users\YSL0\anaconda3\envs\hgto\Library\bin\libiomp5md.dll. No HGTO file was changed. The workaround
KMP_DUPLICATE_LIB_OK=TRUE was not used.
